                <pb facs="0811" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg717"/>

                <head>No. 459.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Manning.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 116, of the 14th
                    ultimo, relative to the recent troubles at Nogales.</p>
                <p>The Department is pleased to notice the friendly tone of Mr. Mariscal’s private
                    letter to you, and it is hoped that his official note, soon to be written, and
                    the prompt and thorough punishment of Gutierrez will terminate the Nogales
                    incident.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
